DevOps / SRE Interview – Flipkart

Round 1 – System Behavior (45 min)

• Your system is stable at normal traffic but starts failing during spikes. What changes internally?
• Your service depends on 3 downstream services. One becomes slow. What happens end-to-end?
• Cache is enabled, but DB load is still high. What could be wrong?
• Your API latency suddenly increases without CPU/memory spike. Why?

⸻

Round 2 – Production Debugging (60 min)

• Deployment succeeded, but error rate increased. Where do you start?
• Some users face issues, others don’t. What could cause this?
• Autoscaling added more pods, but performance didn’t improve. Why?
• Logs show no errors, but system is slow. What do you check next?

⸻

Round 3 – Real Engineering Thinking (30 min)

• How do you design systems to avoid cascading failures?
• How do you identify the first bottleneck in a failing system?
• How do you reduce impact during partial failures?

⸻

💡 Reality

Interviews don’t test:

• tools
• commands
• definitions

They test:

• how systems behave under load
• how failures spread
• how you think under pressure

⸻

That’s where most engineers struggle.

Because they prepare tools…

but not system behavior.
